# OAuth Configuration for Continuum Desktop App
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your credentials:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit .env to git!
#
# =============================================================================
# OAuth Flow Information
# =============================================================================
# The desktop app uses a 3-tier fallback OAuth flow:
#
# 1. LOCAL SERVER (Primary): Opens OAuth in browser, redirects to http://127.0.0.1
#    - Works reliably with all providers
#    - Port is dynamically allocated (except Zoom which requires fixed port 8085)
#
# 2. MANUAL ENTRY (Fallback): User copies authorization code manually
#    - Used when local server fails (port blocked, etc.)
#    - NOTE: Google deprecated OOB flow (urn:ietf:wg:oauth:2.0:oob) in 2022
#    - For Google, use the local server method or deep links
#
# 3. DEEP LINKS (Not supported by most providers for desktop apps)
#    - Google, GitHub, and Zoom require loopback IP (http://127.0.0.1)
#    - Custom URI schemes (continuum://) are NOT supported for desktop OAuth
#
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# Google OAuth (Desktop app type)
# =============================================================================
# Get credentials from: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# 1. Create a new project or select existing
# 2. Enable Google+ API (for profile info)
# 3. Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID with "Desktop app" type
# 4. Copy Client ID and Client Secret below
CONTINUUM_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
CONTINUUM_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret

# =============================================================================
# GitHub OAuth
# =============================================================================
# Get credentials from: https://github.com/settings/developers
# 1. Click "New OAuth App" or select existing app
# 2. Set Homepage URL (e.g., https://continuum.app)
# 3. Set Authorization callback URL to: http://127.0.0.1
# 4. Copy Client ID and generate a Client Secret
CONTINUUM_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your-github-client-id
CONTINUUM_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=your-github-client-secret

# =============================================================================
# Zoom OAuth (General app - User OAuth)
# =============================================================================
# Get credentials from: https://marketplace.zoom.us/develop/create
# 1. Create a "General app" with User-managed OAuth
# 2. Set OAuth redirect URL to: http://127.0.0.1:8085
# 3. Add http://127.0.0.1:8085 to OAuth allow list
# 4. Add scope: user:read:user
# 5. Copy Client ID and Client Secret
#
# IMPORTANT - ZOOM DEVELOPMENT MODE RESTRICTIONS:
# - Unpublished Zoom apps ONLY work for the app creator's account
# - Other users will get "App is not published" or similar errors
# - To add testers: Zoom Dashboard > App > Manage > Add Collaborators
# - To enable all users: Publish app through Zoom Marketplace review process
#
# IMPORTANT - ZOOM REQUIRES FIXED PORT:
# - Unlike Google/GitHub, Zoom requires EXACT redirect URI match
# - Port 8085 is hardcoded - your redirect URI MUST be http://127.0.0.1:8085
# - If port 8085 is in use, Zoom OAuth will fail
CONTINUUM_ZOOM_CLIENT_ID=your-zoom-client-id
CONTINUUM_ZOOM_CLIENT_SECRET=your-zoom-client-secret
